---
title: The Saturday market: indoors or out?
---
- The Saturday market: indoors or out?
  - More than a 40% chance of rain at noon on Friday?
    - Is the church hall free on Saturday? {.from label=yes}
      - Move indoors: the hall takes 18 of the 24 stalls, and the food stalls go under the awning {.from label=yes}
      - Put it off a week, and text every stallholder by 6 pm {.from label=no}
    - Wind over 30 km/h in the forecast? {.from label=no}
      - Outdoors without the gazebos, a sandbag on every table leg {.from label=yes}
      - Outdoors as usual: set up from 7 am, open 9 to 2 {.from label=no}
  - Ruth Ellis decides by 1 pm on Friday and puts it on the market’s page

---
title: No internet at home
---
- No internet at home
  - Does any other phone or laptop get online?
    - Only this one is stuck: turn its wifi off and on, then forget the network and join again {.from label=yes}
    - Is the internet light on the router white? {.from label=no}
      - The line is fine and the wifi is not: switch the router off at the wall for thirty seconds {.from label=yes}
      - Restart the router and wait three minutes: is the light white now? {.from label=no}
        - Back online; if it happens again, note the time for the provider {.from label=yes}
        - Does the provider’s status page, on a phone’s data, show a fault nearby? {.from label=no}
          - Wait it out: the page says when it will be mended {.from label=yes}
          - Call the provider with the account number from the bill: NH-48213-07^[The lines are open 8 am to 8 pm; the wait is shortest before 10.] {.from label=no}
